# Bring-up → Smoke → Verify (must follow)

**Before any code or “it works” claim:**
1) Run `bash scripts/bring_up.sh && bash scripts/smoke_youtube.sh`
   - If either fails, STOP. Fix only that failing step. Re-run both.
2) When both pass, bind UI to the proven endpoints (no direct container calls).

## Use these seams (single source of truth)
- GET /api/health  (+ /api/health/full if present)
- GET /api/tools
- POST /api/runs/youtube/start
- GET /api/runs, /api/runs/{id}, /api/runs/{id}/corpus

## Non-negotiables
- All responses use `{status, data, error}`.
- No disk/tool-registry fallbacks. If MCP/tools are down → return 503 with a clear reason.
- If autosubs are used, record it in metrics and surface it in UI text (no silent fallback).

## Keep context light — point to docs
Before coding, skim:
- ROOT_OVERVIEW.md (endpoints/ports)
- README.md / QUICKSTART.md (health & usage)
- Phase docs for the current scope (e.g., PHASE_8_2_PLAN.md)

## PR checklist (reviewers enforce)
- Pasted outputs of both scripts (“Bring-up & Smoke evidence”)
- One scoped change (backend OR UI, unless trivial glue)
- Minimal tests green
- Docs updated (if behavior/UI changed)
